.TH RRUBOCOP 1 "August 2026" "rrubocop 0.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rrubocop \- fast RuboCop-compatible Ruby linter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rrubocop
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPATH\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
rrubocop is a Rust RuboCop drop-in for Ruby. It parses with tree-sitter and
does not require a Ruby runtime for linting source files. Configuration that
contains ERB still needs
.B ruby
(or
.B bundle exec ruby
) to expand, as with RuboCop. It reads
.B .rubocop.yml
and emits RuboCop-compatible diagnostics.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR
Path to configuration file.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fIFORMAT\fR
Output format: progress, text, json, github, quiet, files, emacs, simple.
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-autocorrect\fR
Apply safe autocorrections.
.TP
\fB\-A\fR, \fB\-\-autocorrect\-all\fR
Apply all autocorrections.
.TP
\fB\-\-only\fR \fICOPS\fR
Run only these cops (comma-separated).
.TP
\fB\-\-except\fR \fICOPS\fR
Exclude these cops.
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-list\-target\-files\fR
List files that would be linted.
.TP
\fB\-\-list\-cops\fR
List registered cop names.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-cache\fR
Disable the on-disk result cache ($RRUBOCOP_CACHE_DIR or ~/.cache/rrubocop).
.TP
\fB\-\-fail\-level\fR \fISEVERITY\fR
Minimum severity for exit code 1 (default: convention).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.BR 0
clean,
.BR 1
offenses,
.BR 2
error.
.SH SEE ALSO
rubocop(1)
